\b The Bible App — User Guide\b0\par
\par
Version: 1.0\par
Last updated: \par
\par
\b Overview\b0\par
The Bible App helps you read Scripture, track progress, and enjoy study tools and games. This guide walks you through the app’s main features, including reading, search, bookmarks, favorites, notes, Verse of the Day, games, and settings.\par
\par
\b Tabs & Navigation\b0\par
- Home: Quick access to Verse of the Day, Prayer/Study Timer, Stopwatch/Focus, and a Resume card to continue reading where you left off.\par
- Bible: Browse books, chapters, and verses. On iPad, a split view shows Books on the left and details on the right.\par
- Search: Search the Bible text (availability and behavior may vary by platform).\par
- Favorites: See verses you have favorited.\par
- Bookmarks: Manage your bookmarked verses.\par
- Notes: Create and edit personal notes attached to specific verses.\par
- Games: Play Hangman with Bible-themed categories.\par
- Settings: Customize appearance and app behavior (where available).\par
\par
\b Home\b0\par
\b1. Verse of the Day\b0\par
- The Verse of the Day automatically refreshes twice a day at 6:00 AM and 6:00 PM.\par
- Tap the Verse of the Day card to open that passage in the Reader.\par
- Actions on the card:\par
  • Copy: Copies the verse and reference to your clipboard.\par
  • Share: Opens the system share sheet.\par
  • Favorite: Toggles the verse in Favorites.\par
- \b Pause/Resume Refresh\b0: Use the Pause button on the card to stop automatic refreshing. While paused, the last shown verse is preserved and also mirrored to widgets (if applicable). Tap again to resume.\par
\par
\b2. Prayer/Study Timer\b0\par
- Start a timer from presets (5, 10, 15, 20, 30 minutes) or choose a custom duration.\par
- While running: Pause/Resume and Stop controls are available.\par
- The app can schedule a local notification when the timer completes.\par
- Live Activities/Dynamic Island (if supported) show progress.\par
\par
\b3. Stopwatch\b0\par
- Start, pause, and stop the stopwatch to track study time.\par
- Stopwatch can appear in Live Activities/Dynamic Island (if supported).\par
\par
\b4. Focus Mode\b0\par
- Enter a Title and Body for your focus.\par
- Tap Save to persist your focus and show it in Live Activities/Dynamic Island (if supported).\par
- Tap Clear to remove the saved focus.\par
\par
\b Resume Reading\b0\par
- The Resume card shows your last reading location (book, chapter, and verse).\par
- Tap the card to jump back into the Reader.\par
\par
\b Bible (Reading)\b0\par
\b1. Books, Chapters, and Verses\b0\par
- On iPad split view (Bible tab):\par
  • Left: Select a Book.\par
  • Right: Select a Chapter, then select a Verse to open the Reader at that verse.\par
- On iPhone (and other compact layouts): Navigate Books → Chapters → Verses using the standard navigation stack.\par
\par
\b2. Reader\b0\par
- Tap a verse to highlight it and set it as your last location (a brief pin icon appears).\par
- Swipe left/right to move to the next/previous chapter.\par
- Long-press a verse to reveal actions: Copy, Share, Note, Bookmark, Favorite.\par
- The app automatically saves reading progress so you can resume later.\par
\par
\b3. Pin Icon\b0\par
- When you tap a verse, a pin icon briefly appears to mark your last location.\par
- The icon uses a red circular head for high visibility.\par
\par
\b4. Notes\b0\par
- Add a note to any verse from the Reader or verse preview.\par
- Notes are stored in the app and accessible from the Notes tab.\par
\par
\b5. Bookmarks\b0\par
- Bookmark a verse to access it quickly later.\par
- Bookmarks appear in the Bookmarks tab.\par
\par
\b6. Favorites\b0\par
- Favorite a verse to add it to your Favorites tab.\par
- Toggle Favorite from the Reader or Verse of the Day card.\par
\par
\b Search\b0\par
- In the iPad split view, use the search field in the Bible detail column.\par
- The search requires at least two words to return results (e.g., "love God").\par
- Results list the book, chapter, and verse; tap a result to open the Reader at that verse.\par
\par
\b Games: Hangman\b0\par
\b1. Overview\b0\par
- Guess the hidden word by tapping letters.\par
- Choose Theme (All, People, Places, Books) and Difficulty (Easy, Medium, Hard).\par
\par
\b2. Difficulty Behavior\b0\par
- Easy: A scripture reference is shown during the round.\par
- Medium: The reference appears after 3 wrong guesses.\par
- Hard: The reference appears only after the round ends.\par
\par
\b3. Scoring and Streaks\b0\par
- Your current session score and streak are shown.\par
- All-time stats (correct, answered, best streak) are tracked per difficulty.\par
\par
\b4. Resetting Game Scores\b0\par
- If there is no in-app reset option available, you can reset all-time stats by deleting and reinstalling the app (this clears the app’s stored data).\par
- Note: Future updates may add an in-app reset in Settings.\par
\par
\b Tips & Tricks\b0\par
- Long-press a verse to quickly copy, share, add a note, bookmark, or favorite.\par
- Use the Resume card on Home to jump back into reading.\par
- Pause Verse of the Day if you want to keep a particular verse visible across refresh times.\par
\par
\b Privacy & Data\b0\par
- Reading progress, favorites, bookmarks, and notes are stored on-device.\par
- Timer/Stopwatch/Focus may use notifications and Live Activities to keep you informed.\par
\par
\b Troubleshooting\b0\par
- \bVerse of the Day didn’t refresh\b0: Ensure it’s not paused. It refreshes at 6:00 AM and 6:00 PM.\par
- \bTimer didn’t alert\b0: Confirm notification permissions in Settings.\par
- \bCan’t find a verse in Search\b0: Enter at least two words. Try broader or alternative phrasing.\par
\par
\b Contact & Feedback\b0\par
We welcome your feedback and suggestions. Please reach out through the App Store contact options or your usual support channel.\par
\par
\b Changelog\b0\par
- Added red pin indicator on verse tap to mark last location.\par
- Improved iPad split view for Books/Chapters/Verses.\par
- Enhanced Hangman difficulty behavior and stats tracking.\par
